      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\nMetformin 2550 mg three times daily comes to 7,650 mg per day. That is three times the maximum recommended daily dose of 2,550 mg (the usual maximum for immediate-release metformin). A dose that high risks serious harm, including lactic acidosis.\n\nYou may have meant one of these:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the maximum daily dose.\n- **A lower dose.** Metformin is usually started at 500 mg once or twice daily with meals, or 850 mg once daily, and increased gradually. Starting at the maximum is uncommon unless the patient is already taking it.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it. Please also confirm the order with your supervising resident or attending."
      }
